Let us consider a family of asymptotic series in the same resurgence class---with the class specified by the constants $\alpha$ and $\beta$ (different sets yielding different classes) and the family $\{ \Phi_{[\gamma]} \}$ parameterized by $\gamma$---which is given by

\begin{equation}
\label{eq:Family-res-funct-app}
\Phi_{[\gamma]} (\lambda) = \lambda^\gamma\, \Phi_{[0]} (\lambda) \simeq \sum_{k=0}^{+\infty} \Phi_k\, \lambda^{\alpha k + \beta + \gamma},
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
D_s^\gamma f(s) = D_s^\alpha D_s^m f(s) = D_s^\alpha\, \frac{{\mathrm{d}}^m f}{{\mathrm{d}} s^m} (s).
\end{equation}
